  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There is a bug in the Vrcavatar Pedestal Set Avatar Use node that is not instantiating something properly when it is on a spawned object.  I've isolated the problem to the node itself by using UItext fields to confirm that a spawned object can see its own avatar pedestal component, as well as the local player\nSteps to reproduce;\nPlace an avatar pedestal on an object, save it as a prefab (My own object that found this test was a held pickup, for full clarity and parity testing if needed).\n  \nSpawn an instance of the prefab.  \n\nThe original version will work, as will any instances of the prefab hand-placed into the world.  The spawned prefab will crash the Udon script and not apply the avatar. \n\nThe script crashing was confirmed with an Update() loop making a UIText display the object's positional coordinates as a held pickup.  Tracked constantly until used, and then froze.",
